## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates understanding of edge cryptography implementation, privacy-preserving design, and business impact analysis in payment systems—skills critical for roles at Cloudflare, Square, and similar fintech companies.

## Key Concepts
- On-device cryptographic verification using Ed25519 and platform crypto APIs
- Key management lifecycle and rotation strategies
- Mobile device constraints: latency, CPU, memory, and energy budgets
- Local telemetry architecture and storage growth patterns
- Regulatory compliance frameworks for payment verification
- Financial modeling with go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify an Ed25519 signature on-device
async function verifyReceipt(receipt, publicKey) {
  // receipt: { data: ArrayBuffer, signature: ArrayBuffer }
  const isValid = await crypto.subtle.verify(
    'Ed25519',
    publicKey,
    receipt.signature,
    receipt.data
  );
  return isValid;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
CBA for an offline-first backup feature requires tangible cost knobs and measurable outcomes beyond accuracy or latency; beginner-friendly but demonstrates ability to quantify trade-offs and plan rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Energy budgeting per photo and dedup impact
- Data minimization and privacy/compliance
- Rollout, offline fallback, drift/maintenance, break-even

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo energy check before upload
function shouldUpload(photoSizeMB, currentEnergyJ, thresholdJ){
  const dedupFactor = 1.5;
  const energyPerMB = 0.25;
  const energy = photoSizeMB * energyPerMB * dedupFactor;
  return (currentEnergyJ - energy) > thresholdJ;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure de-dup effectiveness in production?
- What metrics trigger rollback during rollout?
